        "notes": "Watering: NC State and RHS say keep the mix damp but well drained, mapped to keep_moist. A Clemson pothos guide that appeared in search results (which says to let the soil dry completely) was not fetched, so it is not cited. Severity 1 is the agent's grade (NC State states none; the ASPCA lists dogs and cats as toxic with oral pain, swelling, drooling and vomiting). Size is the RHS cultivar figure (1 to 1.5 m by 0.5 to 1 m); NC State says 1.5 to 3 ft indoors. Humidity: no page gives it."
